# TODO: Verification Plan for Encoding Layer Functions

## Overview

This document describes the TODO plan for verifying the functions and constants
listed in [`doc/truong/encoding.txt`](../truong/encoding.txt), which
enumerates all fully qualified function, trait, and type names from
`src/encoding.rs` (Rust source). These are extracted into
`SrcTranslated/Funs.lean` (Lean 4 / Aeneas extraction).

All extractable functions are configured via
[`aeneas-config.yml`](../../aeneas-config.yml). Functions not appearing in
that configuration (e.g. `#[cfg(test)]` or `#[cfg(feature = "test-utils")]`
items) are not extracted and therefore cannot be verified in the current
framework.

The current Lean specification tree for the encoding layer lives at
[`Spqr/Specs/Encoding/Encoder/`](../../Spqr/Specs/Encoding/Encoder/)
and
[`Spqr/Specs/Encoding/EncodingError/`](../../Spqr/Specs/Encoding/EncodingError/).

The encoding layer is a **thin structural adapter**: it defines the
`Encoder` / `Decoder` trait interface, provides a blanket `Option<T>`
lifting for both traits (using the take/unwrap/delegate/re-wrap pattern
to work around hax limitations with mutable references), and converts
`PolynomialError` into `EncodingError`. No new mathematical content is
introduced at this layer; all substantive logic lives in the polynomial
and GF sub-modules (see [`Plan_poly`](Plan_poly) and
[`Plan_gf`](Plan_gf)).

